{"id":"n3-036","title":"～たところ (〜ta tokoro)","jlptLevel":3,"shortExplanation":"Expresses the result or outcome of an action; 'after', 'just when', 'upon'.","longExplanation":"The ～たところ grammar point is used to indicate the result or outcome right after performing an action. It can be translated as 'after', 'just when', or 'upon' in English. It is formed by attaching ところ to the past tense (た-form) of verbs.","formation":"Verb-た form + ところ","examples":[{"jp":"宿題をしたところ、先生からもう一つ課題が出された。","romaji":"Shukudai wo shita tokoro, sensei kara mou hitotsu kadai ga dasareta.","en":"Just when I finished my homework, the teacher gave us another assignment.","words":[{"surface":"宿題","vocabId":"1337270","reading":"しゅくだい"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"先生","vocabId":"1387990","reading":"せんせい"},{"surface":"から","vocabId":null},{"surface":"もう","vocabId":"2081490","reading":"もう"},{"surface":"一つ","vocabId":"1160820","reading":"ひとつ"},{"surface":"課題","vocabId":"1195820","reading":"かだい"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"出さ","vocabId":"1338180","reading":"だす","baseForm":"出す"},{"surface":"れ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"れる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"友達に会ったところ、彼が海外に行くと言った。","romaji":"Tomodachi ni atta tokoro, kare ga kaigai ni iku to itta.","en":"Upon meeting my friend, he told me he's going abroad.","words":[{"surface":"友達","vocabId":"1540170","reading":"ともだち"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"会っ","vocabId":"1198180","reading":"あう","baseForm":"会う"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"海外","vocabId":"1201260","reading":"かいがい"},{"surface":"に","vocab